  "severity": "Moderate",
  "description": "OpenSSH is an SSH protocol implementation supported by a number of Linux, UNIX, and similar operating systems. It includes the core files necessary for both the OpenSSH client and server.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* openssh: Local MITM of X11 forwarding via abstract UNIX socket pre-binding in Rocky Linux OpenSSH client versions (CVE-2026-55655)\n\n* openssh: Double free in Rocky Linux versions of OpenSSH DH-GEX client path during FIPS known-group validation leads to client-side denial of service (CVE-2026-55653)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
